  partName: Sartorius_muscle_Cranial_part.L
  descriptionChunks:
  - 'The sartorius is a long muscle that functions to flex the hip and extend the
    knee, aiding in forward movement of the limb. It plays a key role in locomotion
    by helping advance the hindlimb. '
  - This muscle also contributes to coordination and balance during movement. It
    works alongside other thigh muscles to ensure smooth and efficient motion. Its
    function is essential for proper gait and controlled limb movement.
